        "body": "_This review was posted by an AI agent (OpenHands)._\n\nReviewed head `d3be8c242aceb7d488772cba4110470b6c720eaf` against base `cc99322`. Verified against the workspace checkout, `AGENTS.md`, and `.agents/skills/custom-codereview-guide.md`.\n\n**Scope:** The PR changes only Canvas-owned developer tooling and contributor guidance (`eslint.config.js`, its two executable flat-config suites, and `.agents/skills/frontend-development/references/guide.md`). This belongs in this repository; no product/architecture decision is needed. Linked issue #19525 is open with `ready-for-dev` and `priority:low`.\n\n**What was verified:**\n- The tree equals base except the four changed files, matching the PR's claim; no source, package, lockfile, or runtime files are touched.\n- `shadcn/no-raw-colors` is promoted to `\"error\"` globally with `allow: legacyColorClasses` preserved verbatim \u2014 all seven exact legacy exceptions remain.\n- The three audited owners keep a single consolidated rule block (`error` + `allow` + `scanAllStrings`); the redundant warn override removal is behavior-preserving because the earlier `src/**` block already applies error there.\n- All eleven newly promoted arbitrary-value owners exist on the head, and the 25-entry error list in `eslint.config.js` matches the 25-entry `it.each` in `__tests__/scripts/arbitrary-values-lint.test.ts` exactly. The guide text (\"Twenty-five migrated owners\") and groupings match the config.\n- The new probe asserting `no-arbitrary-values` severity `[1]` for `text-[#ec4899]` on a non-owner path exercises the documented staged boundary (global warn), so bracketed literals remain on the separate rollout as claimed; severity expectations elsewhere were updated 1\u21922 consistently with the promotion.\n- Test probes run with `evaluateOnly`, so they cannot mutate the working tree; `npm run lint` lints `src` only, so CI's ESLint run is unaffected by the test files.\n- CI on this exact head passes (test-and-build ubuntu/windows, validate-pr-description, check-pr-artifacts, pr-title).\n\n**Evidence:** Lint-policy hardening is a non-functional developer-tooling change; the guide's evidence rules accept command/test output for this class. The PR supplies executed flat-config probe results, the regression-first failure run, full `npm run lint` (177 warnings, zero errors), and base-equality \u2014 and correctly labels the attached image as context rather than evidence. Compliant.\n\n**Checklist for #19525 acceptance:** [x] raw palette / undeclared named colors / SVG-paint guard enforced across source; [x] seven legacy exceptions preserved exactly; [x] class-map scanning retained for exactly the three audited owners; [x] eleven completed owners promoted with probes; [x] unadopted paths still warn; [x] docs updated to match config.\n\nNo eval-path risk: prompts, tool selection, conversation payloads, and terminal behavior are untouched. No new dependencies, so the release-age policy does not apply.\n\n\u2705 APPROVED\n"
      }
